  "content": {
    "id": "p15-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "If $x$ and $y$ are positive numbers, $x^2+y^2$ varies directly as $x+y$ and $y=2$ when $x=2$, find the value of $y$ when $x=\\frac45$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$y=\\frac{12}{5}$.\n\nFind the constant of proportionality, then factorise the resulting quadratic and retain the positive root.",
      "worked": "Write $x^2+y^2=k(x+y)$. When $x=2$ and $y=2$,\n$$\\begin{align*}2^2+2^2&=k(2+2)\\\\8&=4k\\\\k&=2.\\end{align*}$$\nHence $x^2+y^2=2(x+y)$. When $x=\\frac45$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{16}{25}+y^2&=\\frac85+2y\\\\y^2-2y-\\frac{24}{25}&=0\\\\25y^2-50y-24&=0\\\\(5y-12)(5y+2)&=0\\\\y&=\\frac{12}{5}\\text{ or }-\\frac25.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $y>0$, $y=\\frac{12}{5}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 88
  },
